1
00:00:05,940 --> 00:00:09,000
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

2
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:31,480
You're on a move!

3
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,400
Bakura, what have you done to them?

4
00:01:11,640 --> 00:01:12,640
Answer me!

5
00:01:14,780 --> 00:01:18,700
These two delinquents received
exactly what they deserved, Yugi.

6
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:22,157
They took possession of something
that didn't belong to them.

7
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:25,020
So I banished their souls
to the Shadow Realm.

8
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:28,480
And I'd say the punishment fit the crime.

9
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:31,320
You sent them to the Shadow Realm?

10
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:34,306
You should be showing a
little more gratitude.

11
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:37,580
After all, I've returned your belongings.

12
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:42,020
Well, most of them.

13
00:01:42,300 --> 00:01:43,300
What's that mean?

14
00:01:44,260 --> 00:01:45,340
Take a look.

15
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:50,077
There was one item in your bag of tricks
that I'm not quite ready to part with.

16
00:01:50,160 --> 00:01:54,240
Besides, it did belong to me
at one time. Give it back!

17
00:01:54,480 --> 00:01:56,656
The Millennium Items belong together!

18
00:01:57,020 --> 00:01:58,491
Eventually, they will be.

19
00:01:58,700 --> 00:01:59,530
In the meantime,

20
00:01:59,613 --> 00:02:03,757
why don't you concentrate on gathering
the other items instead of pestering me?

21
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:07,477
And when the time is right, I'll
give you the Millennium Ring.

22
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:11,325
We may not be fond of each other,
but we do share a common goal.

23
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:15,500
We both want all seven items
returned to their resting place,

24
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:18,686
united once again within
the Millennium Stone,

25
00:02:19,140 --> 00:02:21,480
just as they were so long ago.

26
00:02:21,980 --> 00:02:24,680
I don't trust you, and I never will!

27
00:02:25,340 --> 00:02:27,237
I'm collecting the
Millennium Items so I can

28
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:30,202
help the Pharaoh save the
world from destruction!

29
00:02:30,780 --> 00:02:34,309
And I gather you think that I
have a different goal in mind.

30
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:36,249
Believe whatever you wish,

31
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:38,897
but remember I know
things about the past that

32
00:02:38,980 --> 00:02:42,140
your Pharaoh friend seems
to have forgotten. Oh yeah?

33
00:02:42,380 --> 00:02:44,217
And what kind of things are those?

34
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:48,197
I know that when the seven Millennium
Items are returned to the stone,

35
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:50,633
a doorway to the Spirit World will open.

36
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:52,200
The spirit world?

37
00:02:52,420 --> 00:02:56,157
If that exists, it could be where
the spirit of the pharaoh belongs.

38
00:02:56,240 --> 00:03:00,397
Are you saying that when this doorway
opens, the pharaoh will be set free?

39
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:01,900
You're catching on.

40
00:03:02,160 --> 00:03:04,237
So don't you want to help your friend?

41
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:08,320
After all, his spirit's been trapped
in that puzzle for 5,000 years.

42
00:03:08,660 --> 00:03:09,620
Of course I do!

43
00:03:10,980 --> 00:03:12,280
Yu-Gi-Oh!

44
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:15,480
That's enough!

45
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:17,660
Stop poisoning Yu-Gi's mind!

46
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:20,980
Ah, Pharaoh, to what do I owe this honor?

47
00:03:21,460 --> 00:03:24,997
Did you come here so we can bury
the hatchet and join forces?

48
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:26,640
You know better than that!

49
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:28,440
I know why you hate me.

50
00:03:28,660 --> 00:03:30,757
Because when you get right down to it,

51
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:33,417
you and I are more alike
than you'd care to admit.

52
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:35,029
Isn't that right, Pharaoh?

53
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:36,840
We are nothing alike!

54
00:03:37,620 --> 00:03:40,640
We're both 5,000-year-old
spirits, aren't we?

55
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:44,018
Each one inhabiting the body
of an innocent civilian.

56
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:48,280
The only difference is I remember my past.

57
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:52,040
All your mind contains is an
endless labyrinth of questions.

58
00:03:52,580 --> 00:03:55,897
Your whole life is nothing more
than a puzzle wrapped in a game.

59
00:03:55,980 --> 00:03:58,000
And I happen to know the solution.

60
00:03:58,360 --> 00:04:00,200
It's quite ironic, actually.

61
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:05,320
The only way you can solve
that game is by playing a game.

62
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:09,760
I don't know if you speak the truth,
but I'll do whatever I have to.

63
00:04:10,700 --> 00:04:14,380
Game or no game, I will unlock my mind.

64
00:04:14,720 --> 00:04:16,280
Well then, best of luck.

65
00:04:16,540 --> 00:04:20,128
You're going to need it when
the Ultimate Shadow Game begins.

66
00:04:20,220 --> 00:04:22,240
Enjoy your travels, Farrow.

67
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:28,440
That encounter went exactly as planned.

68
00:04:28,900 --> 00:04:30,800
Now on to Phase 2.

69
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:45,180
Oh, great.

70
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:47,360
The power is completely dead.

71
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:54,259
It's been quite a while, hasn't it?

72
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:56,640
Can I help you with something?

73
00:04:59,540 --> 00:05:00,370
Mogumar!

74
00:05:00,453 --> 00:05:02,257
I don't think he can hear you, Kaiba.

75
00:05:02,340 --> 00:05:05,477
But perhaps if you came up here
with your cards and your dual disc,

76
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:07,972
you'd have a bit more luck communicating.

77
00:05:08,960 --> 00:05:09,790
No!

78
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:18,940
If that freak wants a duel, I'll
give him one he'll never forget.

79
00:05:34,580 --> 00:05:35,410
Mokuba!

80
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:39,260
I would tell you where his soul is,

81
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:41,857
but you don't believe in
the Shadow Realm, right?

82
00:05:41,940 --> 00:05:44,764
Whatever you did to my
brother, you better undo.

83
00:05:45,100 --> 00:05:46,840
Do you understand me, Bakura?

84
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:49,800
As soon as I defeat you, I want him back.

85
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:52,432
Now let's get your little game over with.

86
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:54,980
As you wish.

87
00:05:55,300 --> 00:05:57,300
You're about to regret this.

88
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:01,800
We'll see.

89
00:06:02,760 --> 00:06:03,590
Let's duel.

90
00:06:06,620 --> 00:06:08,600
Now for the fun part.

91
00:06:13,460 --> 00:06:14,380
What's wrong?

92
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:16,955
There's no such thing as magic, right?

93
00:06:17,180 --> 00:06:21,897
And all those ancient visions you've been
having, they don't exist either, do they?

94
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:24,120
Not that Egyptian speech again.

95
00:06:24,420 --> 00:06:28,008
When are you people gonna realize
that I focus on the future?

96
00:06:28,460 --> 00:06:31,800
I don't waste my time
worrying about the past.

97
00:06:33,140 --> 00:06:38,660
That attitude of yours hasn't changed
in over 5,000 years. That's enough!

98
00:06:39,080 --> 00:06:41,840
Just give me a little time, Seto Kaiba.

99
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:44,200
I'll make a believer out of you.

100
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:47,080
Before this shadow game comes to a close,

101
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:50,017
not only will you accept
your ancient heritage,

102
00:06:50,100 --> 00:06:52,720
you'll long to return to your roots.

103
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:55,820
Let the game commence.

104
00:06:56,340 --> 00:06:57,360
My move.

105
00:06:57,740 --> 00:06:58,800
First I'll play...

106
00:06:59,820 --> 00:07:00,702
Polymerization.

107
00:07:01,100 --> 00:07:05,280
fusing my earl and my knight
to form the Duke of Jemais!

108
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:10,400
But the rules forbid me to attack you.

109
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:14,440
I suppose you got off easy
this time, Kaiba. Please.

110
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:19,037
It'll take a lot more than a rotting
carcass with a sword to intimidate me.

111
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:20,840
Now watch how it's done!

112
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:23,960
I summon my Virus Raider in attack mode!

113
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:27,910
Sorry,

114
00:07:28,020 --> 00:07:32,720
but it seems your monster's a few
points shot I'm not done Next,

115
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:36,277
I'll activate this It's my shrink card And

116
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:38,889
it cuts your corpse's
attack points in half

117
00:07:41,700 --> 00:07:43,880
Force Raider, attack now!

118
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:52,900
My attack may not have
destroyed your monster

119
00:07:53,400 --> 00:07:56,160
But it did remove 900 of your life points.

120
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:57,580
Ha ha ha ha!

121
00:07:57,980 --> 00:07:59,717
And you think that worries me?

122
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:02,320
I wouldn't be laughing if I were you.

123
00:08:02,500 --> 00:08:03,600
And why is that?

124
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:05,300
Well, for one,

125
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:09,277
you're about to lose another 500 of
your life points thanks to your friend,

126
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:10,520
the Duke of Demise.

127
00:08:10,820 --> 00:08:12,740
Is that reason enough for you?

128
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:16,300
No, because I have something
far worse in store.

129
00:08:16,940 --> 00:08:22,460
First, I'll sacrifice my Duke in
order to summon my dear bound colonel.

130
00:08:22,900 --> 00:08:25,880
Then I activate the magic
card Spirit Illusion.

131
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:28,631
It creates what's known as a doppelganger,

132
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:33,428
an exact duplicate of my monster, complete
with all the power of the original.

133
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:35,610
Wow.

134
00:08:35,820 --> 00:08:38,140
So now you've got two useless monsters.

135
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:40,800
We'll see about that.

136
00:08:41,280 --> 00:08:43,660
Go, doppelganger, diavau!

137
00:08:45,320 --> 00:08:48,840
Did I forget to mention my
doppelganger's special ability?

138
00:08:49,420 --> 00:08:50,977
Whenever it strikes,

139
00:08:51,060 --> 00:08:55,825
your monster automatically loses attack
points equal to those of my doppelganger.

140
00:08:58,200 --> 00:09:02,100
That leaves your Voseraider in
quite a compromising position.

141
00:09:04,400 --> 00:09:07,040
Now, dearbound colonel, attack!

142
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:15,440
Next, I'll place this face down.

143
00:09:15,780 --> 00:09:16,857
That ends my turn.

144
00:09:16,940 --> 00:09:19,000
No more Mr. Nice Guy!

145
00:09:19,280 --> 00:09:20,480
I play this!

146
00:09:20,780 --> 00:09:22,060
Lord of Dragons!

147
00:09:23,940 --> 00:09:25,640
It's just as I planned.

148
00:09:26,180 --> 00:09:29,180
As long as my Lord of
Dragons is on the field,

149
00:09:29,380 --> 00:09:32,674
any dragon I play is safe
from all magic and trap cards.

150
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:36,560
Therefore, I activate the
Flute of Summoning Dragon!

151
00:09:38,340 --> 00:09:40,811
When both of these cards are on the field,

152
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,780
I can summon any two dragons from my hand!

153
00:09:46,280 --> 00:09:47,110
Excellent

154
00:09:47,580 --> 00:09:48,410
Actually,

155
00:09:48,620 --> 00:09:49,897
now that I think of it,

156
00:09:49,980 --> 00:09:54,560
there's only one dragon that I
need My blue-eyes, white dragon

157
00:09:56,040 --> 00:09:59,517
That's just the card
I hoped you'd play Now

158
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:02,306
it's time for a little
stroll down memory lane

159
00:10:06,060 --> 00:10:07,460
What's going on?

160
00:10:12,160 --> 00:10:14,300
What has he done to you, Kisara?

161
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:20,140
In the name of the
pharaoh, I will save thee

162
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:24,880
Oh no!

163
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:26,640
It's that vision again!

164
00:10:35,360 --> 00:10:40,360
My mind's playing tricks on me again
Just like when I dueled against Yugi

165
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:45,177
Neither of our god cards
will give up You're

166
00:10:45,260 --> 00:10:47,980
right It must be a holographic malfunction

167
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:07,280
This can't be real!

168
00:11:13,980 --> 00:11:17,220
My Millennium Puzzle
transported us to another place.

169
00:11:17,680 --> 00:11:20,940
Perhaps another time. What? But how?

170
00:11:21,540 --> 00:11:23,893
This has to be some kind of an illusion.

171
00:11:24,040 --> 00:11:26,216
We were just in the middle of a duel.

172
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:32,480
Something about this place
seems familiar to me.

173
00:11:32,860 --> 00:11:35,742
Could it be possible that
we're in ancient Egypt?

174
00:11:42,140 --> 00:11:44,300
I'm not falling for that nonsense.

175
00:11:44,740 --> 00:11:48,034
Whatever happened in the past
has nothing to do with me.

176
00:11:48,740 --> 00:11:50,320
Kaiba, something wrong?

177
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:52,249
Are you feeling all right?

178
00:11:55,020 --> 00:12:01,417
i've never felt better now let's get back
to the duel shall we all right blue eyes

179
00:12:01,500 --> 00:12:04,557
destroy his dear bound white lightning

180
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:10,100
attack not so fast i
activate my spirit shield

181
00:12:12,280 --> 00:12:16,377
no way i'm afraid so thanks to my shield

182
00:12:16,460 --> 00:12:18,477
your attack didn't get
anywhere near my dear

183
00:12:18,560 --> 00:12:21,737
bound And all I had to do was extract one

184
00:12:21,820 --> 00:12:24,980
monster from my graveyard
and remove it from play.

185
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:28,897
So as long as I can keep a fresh
supply of creatures in my graveyard,

186
00:12:28,980 --> 00:12:30,451
your attacks are useless.

187
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:33,740
In simpler terms, my life
points are untouchable.

188
00:12:34,100 --> 00:12:35,340
Yeah, maybe for now.

189
00:12:35,520 --> 00:12:36,900
But that won't last.

190
00:12:37,120 --> 00:12:40,120
I place one card face
down and end my turn.

191
00:12:40,600 --> 00:12:45,320
Soon the power of Kaiba's Blue-Eyes
White Dragon will rest in my hands.

192
00:12:46,980 --> 00:12:49,940
I'll begin my turn by
activating the magic card,

193
00:12:50,100 --> 00:12:54,117
Part of Greed That allows
me to draw two more cards

194
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:58,060
from my deck And one of them
happens to be Greed Tablet

195
00:13:03,180 --> 00:13:04,960
What'd you do to my monster?

196
00:13:07,020 --> 00:13:09,897
Your Lord of Dragons, along
with all of its powers,

197
00:13:09,980 --> 00:13:13,377
has been sealed away in that
stone tablet and there's

198
00:13:13,460 --> 00:13:16,897
only one way to set it free
you must shatter the stone

199
00:13:16,980 --> 00:13:20,557
however once my grief tablet
is destroyed you'll receive

200
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:26,700
500 points of damage now my
doppelganger weaken his dragon

201
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:36,540
my blue eyes all righty about attack

202
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:41,680
I activate Attack Guidance Armor!

203
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:50,430
Fine.

204
00:13:50,513 --> 00:13:51,676
You're safe for now.

205
00:13:51,900 --> 00:13:55,540
I'll end my turn by placing two
cards face down on the field.

206
00:13:55,880 --> 00:13:57,380
It's all over for you.

207
00:13:59,460 --> 00:14:01,960
I can sense your fear, Kaiba.

208
00:14:03,120 --> 00:14:06,238
You're gonna pay for what
you did to Mokuba, you rat.

209
00:14:06,540 --> 00:14:09,952
No one messes with the Kaiba
family and gets away with it.

210
00:14:10,080 --> 00:14:13,960
It's time to turn this duel
around by playing Card of Demise.

211
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:16,440
It lets me draw four cards.

212
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:19,780
And after five turns, my
hand goes to the graveyard.

213
00:14:20,680 --> 00:14:23,180
Are you forgetting about my spirit shield?

214
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:26,120
Nothing you draw can damage me.

215
00:14:26,540 --> 00:14:28,780
I'm afraid I'm gonna have to disagree.

216
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:31,220
Now I activate Soul Release.

217
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:33,557
You know what that means, don't you?

218
00:14:33,640 --> 00:14:36,857
I can remove up to five
cards from your graveyard,

219
00:14:36,940 --> 00:14:40,340
and without your monsters
to fuel its power,

220
00:14:40,580 --> 00:14:42,462
your spirit shield is destroyed!

221
00:14:47,680 --> 00:14:51,940
Next, I'll use Silent Doom to bring
back a monster in defense mode,

222
00:14:52,180 --> 00:14:54,360
and I choose Force Raider!

223
00:14:55,980 --> 00:14:59,440
Then I'll sacrifice Force
Raider and my blue eyes!

224
00:14:59,920 --> 00:15:03,214
That's the only way I can get
my dragon's strength back!

225
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:08,040
Blue-Eyes White Dragon, return!

226
00:15:09,860 --> 00:15:11,260
So what's your point?

227
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:15,539
The mighty Blue-Eyes has been reborn
and I'm supposed to run in fear?

228
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:19,680
You will when he attacks your little
snake boy with white lightning!

229
00:15:26,020 --> 00:15:30,117
Not bad, but not good
enough to defeat me, Kaiba!

230
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:36,240
I activate my mirror tablet trap card,
then I activate my rebirth tablet,

231
00:15:36,620 --> 00:15:39,080
so say hello to an old friend.

232
00:15:42,580 --> 00:15:43,410
What?

233
00:15:43,860 --> 00:15:48,200
My rebirth tablet was activated as
soon as my Deerbound was destroyed.

234
00:15:48,680 --> 00:15:52,151
That allowed me to immediately
bring him back to the field.

235
00:15:52,540 --> 00:15:54,840
But wait, there's more.

236
00:16:00,860 --> 00:16:04,020
After you sacrificed your
blue-eyes white dragon,

237
00:16:04,480 --> 00:16:08,040
my mirror tablet was able to
absorb half its attack points.

238
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:11,300
Then they were graciously
donated to my Deerbound,

239
00:16:11,660 --> 00:16:14,700
making him the strongest
monster on the field.

240
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:18,920
Say farewell to your blue-eyes.

241
00:16:19,060 --> 00:16:21,320
Deerbound, destroy him now!

242
00:16:28,020 --> 00:16:29,760
Sorry, but no dice.

243
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:32,500
I activate Monster Reborn!

244
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:36,380
Blue Eyes is back!

245
00:16:37,060 --> 00:16:40,880
Oh, if he only knew what my
Diabound has just accomplished.

246
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:46,740
By destroying his Blue Eyes, it was able
to duplicate and absorb its attack power.

247
00:16:47,220 --> 00:16:49,000
I'd say mission accomplished.

248
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:55,997
Oh well, I guess you're in luck.

249
00:16:56,080 --> 00:17:01,600
You see, Kaiba, I have some other
business to attend to. You're joking!

250
00:17:01,900 --> 00:17:04,077
